<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · river</p><h1 class="enc-title">Brenta</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Brenta is a river of north-eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a>, about 174 km long, rising in the lakes of Caldonazzo and Levico in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/trentino">Trentino</a>. It flows through the Valsugana and past Bassano and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/padua">Padua</a> to the Adriatic south of the Venetian lagoon. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/venice">Venice</a> diverted its mouth to protect the lagoon, and Venetian nobles built villas along its lower course.</p></div>
